uming the big blind is 100 (common in early stages), then 100 is valid.\n\nAlternatively, checking (0) lets you see the turn cheaply and avoid building the pot with a marginal hand.\n\nBut given you raised pre-flop, continuing with a small bet makes sense to represent strength and take down the pot if they missed.\n\nReason:  \nYou should make a small continuation bet to represent strength and potentially win the pot immediately. Your hand has some showdown value but is vulnerable. Betting 100 is low-risk and may induce folds from weaker hands like KJ, Q-10, or underpairs below 8s. It also helps balance your range and maintains aggression from your pre-flop raise. Going all-in (-2) is excessive with just a pair of 8s. Folding (-1) gives up too easily. Checking (0) is passive and lets opponents realize equity cheaply.\n\nAnswer: 100'}
